AKEDORE Next kernel 4.19 for POCO F1 (beryllium)
================================================

  Custom Linux 4.19.325 kernel for the POCO F1, for 4.19 ROMs.
  Based on Aozora 4.19 by Kaiyaa77. Formerly "fsociety kernel".
  AKEDORE comes from the Lamaholot language (East Flores): "don't copy".
  But go ahead and copy it, it's GPL. Lmao.

Builds
------

  KSU        ReSukiSU v4.2.0-rc3 (35171), with or without SUSFS v2.3.0
  NoSU       no root (for Magisk or no root)

  Standard   GPU stock 710 MHz
  AutoBoost  GPU 710 MHz, boosted to 802 MHz while gaming

  Latest source: AKEDORE Next v1, branch akedore-next.
  Zips: AKEDORE-Next-4.19-<NoSU|ReSukiSU|ReSukiSU-SUSFS>-v1.zip
  (older AKEDORE v1 zips: AKEDORE-4.19-*-v1.zip).

  Tested on: OxygenOS 16 port (A16), PixelOS 17 and RestOS 17 (A17),
  Infinity-X 4.1 (A17).

Version name (why it says 5.10.245)
-----------------------------------

  uname shows 5.10.245-akedore-next-v1-KSU, but this is a 4.19 kernel.
  The real base is Linux 4.19.325. The 5.10.245 text comes from Aozora:
  its top Makefile sets KERNELVERSION = 5.10.245 (commit 1caca3f39a19
  by Kaiyaa77, "Makefile: spoof KERNELVERSION string to 5.10.245").
  We kept it as it is and only changed the suffix. Nothing else in the
  kernel is 5.10. Only the version text is changed, not the code.

Install
-------

  Flash the zip in recovery (back up boot first). 4.19 ROMs only:
  the zip refuses to flash on a 4.9 ROM.

Fixes
-----

  - Standby drain: SoC deep sleep works again (~45 mA screen off).
  - Xiaomi thermal profile and charging temperature limit now work.
  - Phone powering off on reboot: fixed (tested 10-15 reboots).
  - USB not detected after replug: fixed (tested 10-15 replugs).
  - USB file transfer menu on PD laptop ports: fixed.
  - Chrome/Brave crash and bpfloader bootloop on Android 17: fixed.
  - Vibrations >= 1 s, QC2 thermal typo, PD/PPS charging at 25 mA.
  - Battery jumps / shutdown with charge left: fuel gauge fix included
    (4.9 parity), not proven on the affected phones yet.
  - Also in v1: Jiro features, USB / reboot / QC fixes, NetHunter
    Wi-Fi driver (rtl8812au), FCC 3.3 A like Infinity-X.

Extras
------

  - Standard can boost too: set gpu_autoboost to 1, or pick Gaming
    in the control module.
  - Eco / balanced / game profiles, lower CPU limits with screen off,
    TCP BBR. Settings: /sys/module/fsociety/parameters/.

Notes
-----

  - Double-tap-to-wake on a non-original LCD works only with AOD on.
  - Build: ./build_akedore.sh [ksu|nosu]. Details: CHANGELOG.md.

